Per-engine curl_cffi impersonate target from settings.yml (`impersonate:`
in an engine's entry). Upstream only lets an engine's own request() set
it; which target a site lets through depends on the egress (from som,
2026-11: Brave only chrome*_android, Yahoo only safari2601). Upstream
discussion of making the target configurable:
https://github.com/searxng/searxng/issues/6931

diff --git a/searx/search/processors/online.py b/searx/search/processors/online.py
index ee92dedf1..7b08f983f 100644
--- a/searx/search/processors/online.py
+++ b/searx/search/processors/online.py
@@ -148,6 +148,11 @@ class OnlineProcessor(EngineProcessor):
 
         params: OnlineParams = {**default_request_params(), **base_params}
 
+        # settings.yml `impersonate:` per engine (hyperconfig patch, searxng#6931); an
+        # engine's own request() still overrides it.
+        if getattr(self.engine, "impersonate", None):
+            params["impersonate"] = self.engine.impersonate
+
         headers = params["headers"]
 
         # add Accept-Language header
